Modifications provide an inference-only text module, explicit request-owned
hybrid state, strict target configuration and standalone weight loading.
The runtime does not invoke Transformers model forward/generate methods.
Transformers remains used for tokenization and as an independently executed
test reference. Model weights retain their own upstream license.

The dedicated FP8 Triton kernel adapts the blockwise E4M3 quantization and
matrix multiplication from Hugging Face's finegrained-fp8 kernel, Apache-2.0:
https://huggingface.co/kernels/kernels-community/finegrained-fp8/tree/0e5764aa5c27d0f005117a92645156481540950a/build/torch-cuda
Modifications specialize dynamic activation quantization, fixed launch geometry
and FP32 accumulation for the dedicated text engine; no Hub kernel download or
Transformers model execution is required by the native runtime.
